00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:00.789 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  star wars fans got plenty of the things  they expected from the first teaser  trailer for the upcoming obi-wan kenobi  series set to debut on disney plus in  may fans have known since august 2019  that ewan mcgregor would be reprising  his role as the jedi master along with  hating christensen's return as darth  vader since the project was announced a  few years ago  hello there  however there were a few surprises in  the obi-wan kenobi trailer some fans  never expected chief among them were the  appearance of the inquisitors the  inquisitors are an order of  force-sensitive hunters that were  trained by darth vader in order to  capture kill or corrupt any surviving  jedi in the galaxy many of them appear  in star wars series like star wars  rebels as well as various related comics  and video games like star wars jedi  fallen order despite their popularity as  villains this is the first time that  they've appeared in a live-action  context similar to cad bane's appearance  on the book of boba fett however not  every star wars fan who watched rebels  is jumping for joy at the inquisitor's  live-action debut in fact it's the  appearance of the grand inquisitor that  has some fans scratching their heads  fans on reddit made it clear that this  live action grand inquisitor was close  to the version of the character we see  in star wars rebels but didn't quite  look right one user wrote i realize the  rebels style as a cartoonified stretched  out look but even so i would have  preferred him look a little thinner in  the face  another user observed he definitely  looks less slim than i thought he'd look  in live action  another responded that in rebels he  gives off the air of a diffident  aristocratic fencer i'm not getting that  vibe from him he looks like a haunted  house reject it's worth noting that the  grand inquisitor's species the powens  are notoriously slim and this character  is no exception in rebels he is depicted  as noticeably taller and thinner than  the majority of characters previous  live-action depictions of the powen  species are also extremely slim one  reddit poster wrote first thing i  noticed as well aren't their heads a  little longer too he didn't look much  like the powens from revenge of the sith  in my opinion this of course doesn't  mean that this new portrayal should be  automatically discounted cad bane's  appearance in the book of boba fett also  led to some minor fan outcry but was  overall well liked by at least a portion  of the viewing audience  consider this my final lesson  look out for yourself  now that we've seen what the obi-wan  kenobi version of the grand inquisitor  will look like it's important to go over  who exactly the inquisitors are in the  world of star wars as we mentioned they  are an order of jedi hunters trained by  darth vader to assist him in the jedi  purge following the events of order 66.  while their exact numbers aren't well  known quite a few make appearances in  rebels and other media putting aside the  grand inquisitor one of the other  inquisitors we see rendered in live  action for the very first time is the  fifth brother played by sung kang he is  the helmet sporting gentleman leading a  squad of stormtroopers at the one minute  15 second mark in the teaser trailer  he's also one of these several  inquisitors to make multiple appearances  in rebels another is riva a brand new  inquisitor whose story is thus far  unknown considering that she hasn't yet  made an appearance in any other star  wars media her fate is the most  ambiguous of the characters we've seen  in the trailer then of course there's  the grand inquisitor the leader of the  bunch who terrorized kanan jarrus and  ezra bridger on multiple occasions in  rebels a former jedi the grand  inquisitor is about as dangerous as the  empire gets without vader getting  involved  in other words his involvement in the  events of obi-wan kenobi spells big  trouble for both obi-wan and the young  luke skywalker thankfully that  intimidating presence is present in the  show's trailer we'll just have to wait  and see whether or not the fans will be  able to overcome his new look  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite star wars characters are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]

